# Copy this to .env, in this same directory, and fill in the two keys.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# It has to sit here, beside onkith and run_live.sh, because that is where
# the app reads it from. Not in ~/, not in the repository root above this
# folder. It is a file called .env, not a directory.
#
# It is read at startup rather than expected in the shell, because the
# device is started from a desktop icon and from boot as well as from a
# terminal, and only the terminal ever had these exported. A launcher
# inherits nothing.
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way. Never commit real values.

# The assistant. Without this the device transcribes and masks correctly
# and says it cannot answer.
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# Music search. Without this "play something" reports that it cannot
# search, and everything else still works.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
YOUTUBE_REGION=SA

# The voice. Kokoro is the one the device ships with; point these at the
# two files install_pi.sh downloads. Both are required - with either one
# missing the voice is skipped in silence and the device falls through to
# piper, espeak and say, sounding wrong rather than reporting anything.
ONKITH_KOKORO_MODEL=/home/pi/onkith-voices/kokoro-v1.0.onnx
ONKITH_KOKORO_VOICES=/home/pi/onkith-voices/voices-v1.0.bin
# Which of Kokoro's voices. Defaults to af_sarah.
# ONKITH_KOKORO_VOICE=af_sarah

# Kokoro costs roughly 600 MB resident and a second or two per sentence
# on a fast laptop. If the Pi cannot hold it, or answers too slowly to
# use, name a lighter voice here and nothing else has to change:
#
#     ONKITH_TTS=piper     needs piper installed and ONKITH_PIPER_MODEL
#     ONKITH_TTS=espeak    always available, robotic
#     ONKITH_TTS=none      silent, everything else still works
#
# ONKITH_TTS=kokoro
# ONKITH_PIPER_MODEL=/home/pi/piper-voices/en_GB-alba-medium.onnx
